# Frontend settings. Copy to .env and fill in.
# Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_ to the browser, so never put secrets here.

# Where the API lives, as the BROWSER should address it.
#
# Leave this empty. The dev server proxies /api to the Express API on port 4000,
# and production serves both behind one proxy (CI-09), so a relative path is
# correct in both. Pointing it at http://localhost:4000 would make the browser
# treat the API as a different site and silently drop the session cookie on
# every request - sign-in appears to work, and then nothing is signed in.
#
# Set it only for a deployment that genuinely splits the two across origins,
# and expect to revisit the cookie's SameSite setting if you do.
VITE_API_URL=
